{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":312745,"num_turns":17,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c485d333-e5bd-4d18-9d1f-94fe46064f57","total_cost_usd":2.2645969999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97934,"cache_read_input_tokens":1405894,"output_tokens":23286,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97934,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":112287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":915},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":23286,"cacheReadInputTokens":1405894,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97934,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2645969999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Edit","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CN5h2EDpmy7ET4JypW6PBy","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/patrik.lindeberg/Claude Code/Axcion AI Repo/ai-resources-diagnostics-workflow/.claude/commands/resolve-repo-problem.md","old_string":"Both modes append a `Status: logged (pending)` entry to `improvement-log.md`, which `/friday-checkup` surfaces for the Friday fix cadence — **when the failure was confirmed and triage produced an actionable repository fix.** The three no-fix outcomes (`not confirmed`, `no action justified`, `transferred`) queue nothing; see MANUAL Step 4 for the table both modes apply.","new_string":"Both modes append a `Status: logged (pending)` entry to `improvement-log.md`, which `/friday-checkup` surfaces for the Friday fix cadence — **when the failure was confirmed and triage ended in one of the three ranked options: Quick patch, Structural fix or Defer.** The three no-fix outcomes (`not confirmed`, `no action justified`, `transferred`) queue nothing; see MANUAL Step 4 for the table both modes apply.","replace_all":false}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Committed as `9a8399c`. Handed back with `turn: codex`.\n\n**What happened.** This was a correction round on task `diagnostics-workflow`, not a new unit — Codex had frozen three findings for me to fix. Two are fixed, one is only half fixed, and I was blocked by a permission problem rather than by anything wrong with the work.\n\n**A thing worth knowing first.** When this run started, the fixes were already sitting in the working tree, uncommitted. An earlier run had done the edits and was cut off before it could record or commit them. I checked every edit against the findings myself instead of trusting it, and committing them is what stopped that work from being lost a second time.\n\n**The three findings.**\n\nFinding 1 (the Direct Work rule contradicted itself) and finding 3 (a transfer example that would not actually run in this checkout) are both fully resolved, in both command files. I confirmed each problem really existed in the last commit before accepting its fix, so the fix is a visible change of state and not just a claim.\n\nFinding 2 (when a \"Defer\" result should go into the Friday queue) is **partly** resolved. The main rule is now settled and says the same thing in both of the command's two modes: a Defer does go into the queue, but does not hand a fix onward. Two older sentences elsewhere in the same file still describe the old, narrower rule, at lines 13 and 206 of `resolve-repo-problem.md`. Someone reading only those two lines would do the wrong thing, so the finding is not closed.\n\n**Why I stopped.** This run was launched by the handoff spike as a background Claude process with normal permissions, so it did not get this repo's usual write access. My first edit to `.claude/commands/resolve-repo-problem.md` was refused. I did not work around the refusal with a shell command, because that would be stepping around a gate you control. I wrote the exact replacement text into the state file so the next run can apply it quickly. This is the same environment blocker that stopped Unit 3.\n\n**One honest gap.** I ran the checks that compare text and files, and they all pass — the schema files are untouched, the command descriptions are unchanged, and the status vocabulary still matches across all five places. But I did not re-run the six real command tests from Unit 4. These corrections change behaviour, so Unit 4's own standard asks for a real test run. I am reporting that as missing rather than letting the text checks stand in for it.\n\n**Next.** Codex decides: either close and accept those two lines as a written limitation, or open one small final fix for them in a session that can write to `.claude/commands/`.","ttft_ms":2811,"ttft_stream_ms":1845,"time_to_request_ms":24,"type":"result","duration_ms":317599,"uuid":"44027c02-9660-4258-a4bb-19f15aa3a5db"}
